gosh seam 21: The pseudo-terminal is a domain, Pty: the stand-ins for forkpty and cfmakeraw, in src/pty.

For:   REQ21/SHAPE-1, the core factored into domains by the seam. pty_compat was in the
       utilities, and the only part of them in no namespace: its two functions stand for the
       system's own where a system lacks them (Solaris, AIX), and seam/DOMAINS allowed them there.
       They are the operating system's side of a terminal, which the programs, one example and
       one test use; not the terminal of src/terminal, which is the emulator and makes no system
       call. The owner, 2026-11-27: "Pty as its own domain".
What:  Moves, and renames of where names are, and nothing else: no byte of the protocol, and no
       behaviour, changes. pty_compat.h and imp/pty_compat.cc move from src/util to src/pty by
       git's renames; my_forkpty and my_cfmakeraw are in Pty, and the macros that stand for the
       system's names (only where the system lacks them) say Pty::. The header includes what its
       declarations name (termios, winsize, pid_t), since a struct first named inside a namespace
       would be that namespace's. Where the system has both, as on Linux and macOS, the file
       compiles to nothing, as before. Pty is built as its own library, libmoshpty.a, linked by
       what uses it.
Where: src/pty/ (new: Makefile.am, pty_compat.h, imp/pty_compat.cc); src/util/Makefile.am;
       src/Makefile.am (SUBDIRS); configure.ac (AC_CONFIG_FILES); src/frontend/Makefile.am,
       src/examples/Makefile.am, src/tests/Makefile.am (what they link); the includes in
       src/frontend/imp/{mosh-server,stmclient}.cc, src/examples/{parse,ntester,termemu}.cc and
       src/tests/inpty.cc.
Kind:  two files moved; their names in Pty; one library added; users' includes changed.
From:  the core at the pin: src/util/pty_compat.h, src/util/pty_compat.cc (moved under imp/ by
       patch 18).
Pin:   upstream mosh at decd9b705eb81626f694335b8d5940538beb06da; cut against the result of the patch before it.

